6. The return of a fit or paroxysm of disease, or fever. In this sense accession is generally used.ACCESSIBIL'ITY, n. The quality of being approachable; or of admitting access.ACCESS'IBLE, a.

1. That may be approached or reached; approachable; applied to things; as an accessible town or mountain.

2. Easy of approach, affable, used of persons.ACCESS'ION, n. L. accessio.

1. A coming to; an acceding to and joining; as a king's accession to a confederacy.

