Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness. Col. i.

8. Opakeness.

Land of darkness, the grave. Job x.D'ARLING, a. Dearly beloved; favorite; regarded with great kindness and tenderness; as a darling child; a darling science.

D'ARLING, n. One much beloved; a favorite; as, that son was the darling of his father.D'ART, n. Gr., a spear or lance.

