8. Manageableness; compliance; obsequiousness.

9. Regularity of behavior. Not in use.

10. Management of the limbs or body. Not in use.

11. In grammar, the influence of a word in regard to construction,as when established usage required that one word should cause another to be in a particular case or mode.GOV'ERNOR, n. He that governs, rules or directs; one invested with supreme authority. The Creator is the rightful governor of all his creatures.

