He sits or studies by himself.

Ahab went one way by himself,and Obadiah went another way by himself. 1 Kings 18.HIN, n. Heb. A Hebrew measure of capacity containing the sixth part of an ephah, or about five quarts English measure.HIND, n. The female of the red deer or stag.

HIND, n. A domestic; a servant.

1. A peasant; a rustic; or a husbandman's servant.

