LOWER, v.i. To fall; to sink; to grow less.LOW'ERINGLY, adv. with cloudiness or threatening gloom.LOWEST, a. superl. of low. Most low; deepest; most depressed or degraded, &c.LOWING, ppr. Bellowing, as an ox.

